  "paragraph": 12,
  "text": "Back in the SWE-agent research paper, Princeton engineers named this discipline the Agent-Computer Interface, or ACI. Tools are not just backend APIs; tools are a user interface designed specifically for a language model. Suppose our agent tries to patch auth.ts and misses a line. A cryptic error like exit code one forces blind guessing. An actionable harness error returns the exact mismatch, prints lines forty through forty-eight for context, and hints at narrowing the edit target so the model recovers on the very next turn.",
